preConditionHook:
// A TWO-BAR REVERSAL AT A LEG EXTREME. The PRIOR bar made a new swingLookback-
// bar low -- its low is at or below lowest(low, swingLookback)[2], the window
// ending just before it, so the bar is not in its own benchmark -- and THIS bar
// is a bull bar closing above the prior close while still reaching back into the
// prior bar's low, within overlapTicks of it. Mirrored at a top.
//
// EL: priorLow = lowest(low, swingLookback)[2];
//     low[1] <= priorLow and close > open and close > close[1] and
//     low <= low[1] + overlapTicks * tickSize
//
// NOT TwoBarReversal, which asks for a bear bar followed by a bull bar closing above
// the two-bar midpoint with a size ratio, and fires ANYWHERE. The new-extreme
// requirement is a different rule, not a threshold: this one fires only at the
// end of a leg. Not BullReversalBarAtNewLow either -- that is a SINGLE bar at
// the new low judged by its close position in its own range; here the extreme
// belongs to the bar BEFORE the signal, which is what makes it two-bar.
//
// THE OVERLAP TERM is what keeps the pair a reversal rather than a gap-up
// continuation: the bull bar must still trade at or near the prior bar's low,
// overlapTicks above it at most.
//
// The swing-pivot language of V01-07 and V24-06 is mechanized as a plain
// lowest/highest window, per the merge (least machinery, no confirmation lag).
// V01-07 uses 10 bars and V24-06 20; default 20.
//
// THE WINDOW IS WRITTEN OUT as the Extremes loop lowest/highest bottom out in --
// seeded at the window's first bar (index 2), scanning the rest with a strict
// comparison. Extremes is EL source, so its comparisons carry the measured
// 2.22e-12 relational tolerance, hence el_lt/el_gt rather than raw < and >;
// only the VALUE is read, so the tie rule (an equal extreme keeps the earliest
// bar) cannot show. The same construction BreakoutClearsPriorExtremeByMargin
// uses, shifted one bar further back.
//
// The tick is written division-first, mirroring EL's MinMove / PriceScale, and
// read once per bar into a local. Every scratch value is a localVariables
// entry, never a hook-scope declaration, so the hooks survive a double
// placement. Deepest bar touched: swingLookback + 1.
tickSize = ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale();
priorLow = low[2];
priorHigh = high[2];
for (int i = 3; i <= (int)swingLookback + 1; ++i) {
    if (el_lt(low[i], priorLow)) priorLow = low[i];
    if (el_gt(high[i], priorHigh)) priorHigh = high[i];
}
